-- Migration 1925 — withdraw 53 same-sex-marriage chairs that a PARAPHRASE decided.
--
-- FOUND BY THE CONTRADICTION CHECK (PR #1085), on its first real queue. 54 members who voted FOR
-- the Respect for Marriage Act, each row resting on that vote, were split across three rungs:
-- **27 at rung 2, 26 at rung 3, 1 at rung 4.** One vote, one bill, three answers.
--
-- 🔴🔴 THE SPLIT IS AN ARTEFACT OF THE SUMMARY, NOT OF THE MEMBERS. Measured over the cluster:
--   rung-3 rows mention the religious carve-out  23 of 26
--   rung-2 rows mention it                        2 of 27, and mention benefits 18 of 27
-- Whichever half of the Act the researcher paraphrased set the chair. Nobody was reading the
-- member; they were summarising the bill, and the summary chose.
--
-- ⚖ THE ENACTED TEXT SETTLES THAT BOTH READINGS ARE TRUE — which is exactly why neither can seat
-- a rung. Public Law 117-228, fetched and read, not taken from the title:
--   SEC. 4  FULL FAITH AND CREDIT GIVEN TO MARRIAGE EQUALITY            -> rung 2's claim
--   SEC. 6(b) "nonprofit religious organizations ... shall not be required to provide services,
--             accommodations, advantages, facilities, goods, or privileges for the solemnization
--             or celebration of a marriage"                             -> rung 3's claim
-- The Act carries both, so a vote for it endorses a package holding both. It proves the SIDE and
-- not the RUNG — the Texas cohort's rule, and "chair_needs_evidence_for_that_chair": evidence
-- establishing only a direction under-determines which chair on that side the person occupies.
--
-- ⚠ WHY NOT RE-SEAT THE CLUSTER TO RUNG 3 INSTEAD. Rung 3 describes the instrument most completely,
-- and that was the live alternative. It was rejected because rung 3 asserts the member wants to
-- "protect religious organizations' right to decline", and a vote for the only available vehicle
-- does not show that — several of these members accepted section 6 as the price of sixty Senate
-- votes. Publishing that as their position would misrepresent them. A blank withdraws a claim
-- nobody established; a re-seat would assert a new one on the same evidence.
--
-- 🔑 A BLANK HERE IS RECOVERABLE. The reasoning and every citation stay on the row, so the research
-- is not lost and any of these can be re-seated the moment a member-specific record is found.
--
-- ⚠ NOT BLANKED — 1 of the 54. **Martin Heinrich** was an ORIGINAL COSPONSOR of legislation to
-- repeal DOMA, which is a second record of his own, carries no section 6(b) ambiguity, and is
-- benefits parity on its face. His chair stands at 2 and this migration does not touch it.
--
-- ▶ RECORDED, NOT ACTED ON — A LADDER REACHABILITY FINDING FOR SEASON 3.
-- "inform.compass_topic_roles" marks same-sex-marriage at FEDERAL level evidence_basis 'record'.
-- The Respect for Marriage Act is the only federal marriage instrument there is, and it carries
-- section 6(b). So for a member of Congress, on a record basis, **rungs 1 and 2 may have no
-- reachable instrument at all** — naming the corpus (federal statute) and the source class
-- (roll-call record), as the reachability rule requires. That is a ladder question, and
-- compass_topic_roles is NOT touched here.
--
-- ⚠ "audit-chair-evidence.mjs" IS A PRE-WRITE GATE FOR ANY MIGRATION THAT SETS A CHAIR, and
-- migration 1921 was applied without it, which is why 1922 had to undo two re-seats. **This
-- migration sets no chair** — every row goes to 0 — so there is no chair for that gate to test.
-- Said explicitly rather than skipped silently.
--
-- 🔑 WHY SEASON 2. Season 1 is closed and is not touched. A blank writes 0, which SUPPRESSES
-- (NULLIF(pa.value, 0)). All 53 rows already serve from Season 2, so all are UPDATEs.
--
-- Applied by hand via psql; no migration runner exists in this repo, so "applied" means its data
-- effects are live. Guards below fail the whole transaction rather than write a partial result.

CREATE TEMP TABLE mig1925_decisions (
  politician_id     uuid NOT NULL,
  topic_id          uuid NOT NULL,
  topic_revision_id uuid NOT NULL,
  value_before      int  NOT NULL,
  reasoning         text NOT NULL,
  ledger_no         text NOT NULL
) ON COMMIT DROP;

INSERT INTO mig1925_decisions
  (politician_id, topic_id, topic_revision_id, value_before, reasoning, ledger_no)
VALUES
